**Defects**

- Lines 30-31, instrument reads a different copy. Exact input: current run writes `F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\scratchpad\rollout.log` containing `1/1 p.html SKIPPED, not a current-generator page (10 words)`, while the hardcoded `F:/claude-temp/.../rollout.log` is absent or stale. Consequence: the audit is detached from the worktree being changed.

- Lines 61-62, absent page is silently dropped. Exact input: hardcoded log contains `1/1 missing.html SKIPPED, not a current-generator page (10 words)`, `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json` is `{}`, and `missing.html` does not exist. Consequence: it exits 0 after examining 0 pages, converting uninspectable evidence into “nothing wrong.”

- Lines 77-82, missing object mapping/object is silently treated as not stale. Exact input: log contains `1/1 p.html SKIPPED, not a current-generator page (10 words)`, `p.html` contains `Endpoint definitions, read from the registry`, and `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json` is `{}` or maps `p.html` to a nonexistent file. Consequence: it can print “none is stale against its object” without checking any object.

- Line 92, pooled-point detection is substring text matching. Exact input: `p.html` visible text is `Endpoint definitions, read from the registry N=10`; mapped object is `{"results":{"by_outcome":{"x":{"pooled":{"point":1}}}}}`. Consequence: `"1" in "N=10"` suppresses the stale finding even though the pooled point is not shown.

- Lines 112-114, status code reports only “stale found,” not “current page wrongly skipped.” Exact input: same as above but page text includes the exact point `1`. Consequence: it exits 0 while reporting a current-generator page was “WRONGLY EXCLUDED FROM THE ROLLOUT.”

No proven finding: idempotency guard satisfied by comment/marker; CRLF/LF text equality; merged-cell/off-by-one; negation dropped; subprocess/pipe wrapper status.
